==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*večerъ}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*wekʷsperos}}. Cognates include Ancient Greek {{term|sc=polytonic|ἕσπερος|tr=hesperos|lang=grc}}, Latin {{term|vesper|lang=la}}, Old Armenian {{term|գիշեր||sc=Armn|tr=gišer|lang=xcl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/'vʲet͡ɕɪr/|lang=ru}}
* {{audio|Ru-вечер.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
'''вечер''' (véčer) {{m}}

# [[evening]]
# [[tonight]], this evening
#: Вечер обещает быть приятным. — Tonight is going to be a pleasant night.
# {{context|formal|lang=ru}} [[party]], [[social]] [[gathering]], [[soiree]]

